WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
The major trade was done from Grand Chenier by water to Lake Arthur or to Galveston [Texas].

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.920
That trade was in . . . Now, I'm going to talk about before my time now.

3
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.120
That's fine.

4
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.960
That trade was with Sea Island Cotton going back to the early part of the century.

5
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:29.980
They had commerce with pecans, commerce with citrus, and probably one of the major money issues as far as currency is concerned was trapping.

6
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.660
There were stores right there along the Mermentau River that did the shipping.

7
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.480
I actually went through Hurricane Audrey in Creole.

8
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.300
And there were cotton gins . . . the old cotton gin was still there near Oak Grove.

9
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:49.760
That was remnant of that cotton period in time.

10
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:59.240
The rows from that cotton and some of the ditching from that cotton are still there today, you know, a hundred years later.

11
00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:04.500
So my family was associated with a piece of land called Mermentau Meadow.

12
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:11.240
It was under a land manager, probably 1930, '31.

13
00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.460
They had hunting people that came in, they hunted basically on the south side of Grand Chenier.

14
00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.820
It was in on the area that was open.

15
00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:22.800
The north marsh was pretty solid.

16
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.580
Solid with Cladium Jamaicense or saw grass.

17
00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:35.060
And until Hurricane Audrey . . . actually until the drought, probably 1951 to 1953, caused a lot of that saw grass to die,

18
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:44.300
and then Hurricane Audrey opened that up to where you had areas that were opened up north of Grand Chenier, Pecan Island, that area.

19
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:54.240
The big burn, you know, was a fire in the twenties that opened up some of the areas between the prairie and the Cheniers.

20
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.920
So it opened up that particular area.

21
00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:01.460
So, you know, I've been involved with the marsh since my earliest remembrance.
